## Server-action auth

`sendo.inbox` runs with the service role and does no auth. Every server action must call your auth check first, and the template’s `requireUser()` throws until you implement it (fail closed):

```ts title="app/(protected)/inbox/actions.ts"
interface AppUser {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string | null;
}

// Fail closed: throw until you wire your app's session check.
async function requireUser(): Promise<AppUser> {
  throw new Error("TODO: requireUser() — return the signed-in staff user or throw.");
}
```

Then pass the user’s tenant to every call. `tenantId` is required for `list`; for `thread`, `reply` and `markSeen` it turns another tenant’s conversation into a `RecordNotFoundError`. `sendo.conversations.*` take no tenant, so check it yourself:

```ts title="app/(protected)/inbox/actions.ts"
export async function listConversations(cursor?: string) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  return sendo.inbox.list({ tenantId: user.tenantId, status: ["human", "agent"], cursor });
}

export async function openThread(conversationId: string, cursor?: string) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  const page = await sendo.inbox.thread(conversationId, { tenantId: user.tenantId, cursor });
  await sendo.inbox.markSeen(conversationId, { tenantId: user.tenantId });
  return { ...page, items: page.items.toReversed() }; // newest first → chronological
}

export async function reply(conversationId: string, payload: InboxReplyPayload) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  return sendo.inbox.reply(conversationId, payload, { userId: user.id, tenantId: user.tenantId });
}

export async function take(conversationId: string) {
  const user = await requireUser();
  await assertSameTenant(conversationId, user);
  return sendo.conversations.assign(conversationId, user.id, { by: user.id });
}
```

- `reply` stores the message as sender `human` with `senderRef` = your user id. Outside the window, free-form replies throw `WindowClosedError` before calling Meta, and the composer switches to the template picker.
- Media URLs in `thread` are signed for 300 seconds; request the thread again rather than storing them.

## The actions contract

`<Inbox actions={...} />` receives the server actions as one object. The page passes the ones in `actions.ts`; you can pass your own implementation (another backend, a test double). Every action resolves to a result instead of throwing, so the inbox can show the right message:

```ts title="components/sendo/types.ts"
export type InboxActionResult<T> =
  | { ok: true; data: T }
  | { ok: false; code: "WINDOW_CLOSED" | "NOT_FOUND" | "INVALID" | "UNKNOWN"; message: string };

export type InboxFilter = ConversationStatus | "all";

export type InboxReplyInput =
  | { kind: "text"; body: string }
  | { kind: "media"; file: File; caption?: string }
  | { kind: "template"; name: string; language: string; variables: string[] };

export interface InboxActions {
  list(input: {
    filter: InboxFilter;
    assignedToMe: boolean;
    cursor?: string | null;
  }): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxPage<InboxConversationView>>>;
  /** Newest first; `nextCursor` loads older messages. */
  thread(
    conversationId: string,
    cursor?: string | null,
  ): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxPage<InboxMessageView>>>;
  reply(
    conversationId: string,
    input: InboxReplyInput,
  ): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxMessageView>>;
  markSeen(conversationId: string): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxConversationPatch>>;
  take(conversationId: string): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxConversationPatch>>;
  returnToAgent(conversationId: string): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxConversationPatch>>;
  close(conversationId: string): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxConversationPatch>>;
  listTemplates(conversationId: string): Promise<InboxActionResult<InboxTemplateView[]>>;
}
```

- `WINDOW_CLOSED` from `reply` switches the composer to the template picker and keeps the draft.
- Failures show a `sonner` toast; successful actions don’t (the badge change is the feedback).

## Realtime and RLS

The migration adds `sendo_conversations` and `sendo_messages` to the `supabase_realtime` publication. Browser clients use your anon key and the user’s session, so they only receive rows for which `sendo_can_access_tenant(tenant_id)` is true. With the default (`false`) the inbox gets no live updates: implement it as in [Quickstart step 4](https://sendo.dev/docs/quickstart#migration).

## Strings

The inbox is in Spanish (es-GT) by default. Every user-facing string comes from one defaults module and can be overridden through a `strings` prop, so you can rephrase or translate without editing the components. Dates use `date-fns` with the `es` locale and the `America/Guatemala` timezone by default (`timeZone` prop).

| Group                     | Keys (examples)                                                                                               |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Conversation list         | `filterHuman, filterAgent, filterClosed, filterAll, assignedToMe, listEmpty, unreadCount(n)`                  |
| Status badge              | `statusHuman, statusAgent, statusClosed`                                                                      |
| Thread                    | `loadOlder, threadEmpty, threadEmptyHint, senderContact, senderAgent, senderHuman`                            |
| Message content and media | `messageTypeLabel(type), messageReaction(emoji), mediaUnavailable, mediaPreviewTitle, sheetClose`             |
| Status ticks              | `tickPending, tickSent, tickDelivered, tickRead, tickFailed, errorCode(code)`                                 |
| Actions and window        | `take, returnToAgent, close, actionFailed, windowOpen(remaining), windowClosed`                               |
| Composer and templates    | `composerPlaceholder, send, sendFailed, templateExplanation, templateOpen, templateVariable(i), templateSend` |

The full list with defaults is `InboxStrings` / `defaultInboxStrings` in `components/sendo/strings.ts`. Some keys are functions (plurals, codes):

```ts title="Overriding strings"
// <Inbox strings={{ ... }} /> — override any key; the rest keep the Spanish defaults.
export const inboxStrings = {
  filterHuman: "Personas",
  take: "Asignarme",
  templateExplanation: "La ventana de 24 horas cerró. Envía una plantilla aprobada.",
