## Motion tokens

Inbox components animate only `transform` and `opacity`, with durations and curves from these custom properties:

```css title="components/sendo/motion.css"
/* sendo inbox motion tokens. Override any of them in your own CSS. See MOTION.md. */
:root {
  --sendo-ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  --sendo-ease-in-out: cubic-bezier(0.65, 0, 0.35, 1);
  --sendo-dur-press: 120ms; /* press feedback 100–160 ms */
  --sendo-dur-fast: 160ms; /* tooltips, small popovers 125–200 ms */
  --sendo-dur-menu: 200ms; /* dropdowns, selects 150–250 ms */
  --sendo-dur-sheet: 320ms; /* dialogs, sheets 200–500 ms */
}

/*
 * Reduced motion keeps the durations, so opacity and colour still fade (they help to follow a
 * state change), and removes movement: every element that moves carries `sendo-motion-transform`,
 * whose transform (rise on enter, press scale) is neutralised here. The mobile sheets are driven
 * by `motion` and switch to an opacity-only fade through `useReducedMotion()`.
 */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .sendo-motion-transform {
    transform: none !important;
  }
}
```

| Token                                    | Used for                                                                                                                                            |
| ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `--sendo-dur-press`                      | Press feedback on Tomar / Devolver / Cerrar and the send buttons (scale 0.97 on pointer-down)                                                       |
| `--sendo-dur-fast`                       | Status badge and status tick cross-fades                                                                                                            |
| `--sendo-dur-menu`                       | New conversation rows and bubbles entering; composer ↔ template picker                                                                              |
| `--sendo-dur-sheet`                      | Reserved for dialogs you add. The mobile sheets (template picker, media preview) use a critically damped motion spring with drag-to-dismiss instead |
| `--sendo-ease-out / --sendo-ease-in-out` | Entering elements / on-screen movement. Never ease-in.                                                                                              |

Override them after importing `motion.css`. Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` the durations stay, so opacity and colour still fade (they help to follow a state change), and movement is removed: every element that moves carries `.sendo-motion-transform`, whose transform (the short rise of new rows and bubbles, the press scale) is neutralised. The mobile sheets read `useReducedMotion()` and only fade, without the slide or the drag handle. The recipes and the reasons behind each one are in the item’s `MOTION.md`.

```css title="app/globals.css"
/* app/globals.css — after importing components/sendo/motion.css */
:root {
  --sendo-dur-menu: 160ms; /* snappier entrances */
  --sendo-ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
}

/* Turn every inbox motion off (opacity and colour changes become instant too). */
.inbox-static {
  --sendo-dur-press: 0ms;
  --sendo-dur-fast: 0ms;
  --sendo-dur-menu: 0ms;
  --sendo-dur-sheet: 0ms;
}
```

## sendo_events (built in)

Every webhook POST is stored raw in `sendo_events` so failed events can be reprocessed. Rows older than 30 days should be deleted. Pick one of the two options below; running both is harmless.

## Option A: pg_cron

If the `pg_cron` extension is enabled when the `sendo-schema` migration runs (Supabase: **Database › Extensions**), the migration schedules a daily job:

```sql title="sql"
-- Scheduled by the sendo-schema migration when pg_cron is installed:
select cron.schedule('sendo_prune_events_daily', '17 3 * * *', 'select public.sendo_prune_events(30)');
```

`sendo_prune_events(days)` deletes events received more than `days` ago and returns the count. It is service-role only. If you enable pg_cron later, or want another period:

```sql title="sql"
-- Enabled pg_cron after applying the migration? Schedule it yourself:
create extension if not exists pg_cron;
select cron.schedule('sendo_prune_events_daily', '17 3 * * *', 'select public.sendo_prune_events(30)');

-- Change the retention, inspect or remove the job:
select cron.unschedule('sendo_prune_events_daily');
select cron.schedule('sendo_prune_events_daily', '17 3 * * *', 'select public.sendo_prune_events(14)');
select * from cron.job where jobname = 'sendo_prune_events_daily';
```

## Option B: Vercel Cron

Without pg_cron, call `sendo.maintenance.prune()` from a scheduled route. It deletes events older than `eventRetentionDays` (default 30) and returns the count; pass `{ olderThanDays }` to override.

```ts title="app/api/cron/sendo-prune/route.ts"
// app/api/cron/sendo-prune/route.ts
import { sendo } from "@/lib/sendo";

export const runtime = "nodejs";

export async function GET(request: Request) {
  // Vercel Cron sends `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET`.
  const secret = process.env.CRON_SECRET;
  if (!secret || request.headers.get("authorization") !== `Bearer ${secret}`) {
    return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
  }
  const deleted = await sendo.maintenance.prune(); // events older than eventRetentionDays
  return Response.json({ deleted });
}
```

```json title="vercel.json"
{
  "crons": [{ "path": "/api/cron/sendo-prune", "schedule": "17 3 * * *" }]
}
```

Set `CRON_SECRET` in the Vercel project; Vercel sends it as a bearer token on cron requests. Any other scheduler (GitHub Actions, Supabase scheduled functions) can call the same route.

## Messages and media (your policy)

Sendo never deletes `sendo_messages`, `sendo_media` or stored files. How long conversations are kept is your app’s decision (and, for health or financial data, often a legal one). A starting point that deletes files through the Storage API and then the messages (their `sendo_media` rows cascade):

```ts title="app/api/cron/sendo-message-retention/route.ts"
// app/api/cron/sendo-message-retention/route.ts — YOUR policy for sendo_messages / sendo_media.
import { createClient } from "@supabase/supabase-js";

const RETENTION_DAYS = 365;
const BUCKET = process.env.SENDO_STORAGE_BUCKET ?? "sendo-media";

export async function GET(request: Request) {
  if (request.headers.get("authorization") !== `Bearer ${process.env.CRON_SECRET ?? ""}`) {
    return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
  }
  const supabase = createClient(
    process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL ?? "",
    process.env.SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY ?? "",
    { auth: { persistSession: false } },
  );
  const cutoff = new Date(Date.now() - RETENTION_DAYS * 86_400_000).toISOString();

  // 1. Delete the stored files first (Storage API, not SQL on storage.objects).
  const { data: media, error } = await supabase
    .from("sendo_media")
    .select("storage_path")
    .lt("created_at", cutoff)
    .not("storage_path", "is", null)
    .limit(1000);
  if (error) throw error;
  const paths = (media as { storage_path: string }[]).map((row) => row.storage_path);
  if (paths.length > 0) await supabase.storage.from(BUCKET).remove(paths);

  // 2. Delete old messages; sendo_media rows cascade.
  const { count } = await supabase
    .from("sendo_messages")
    .delete({ count: "exact" })
    .lt("created_at", cutoff);
  return Response.json({ files: paths.length, messages: count ?? 0 });
}
```

> **Note:**
>
> - Delete files before rows: once the `sendo_media` row is gone you lose the storage path.
> - The sample handles up to 1,000 files per run; schedule it often enough or loop.
> - Deleting messages also removes them from the inbox and from agent history. Archive first if you need an audit trail. See [Security](https://sendo.dev/docs/security).

## Accounts and tenants

One deployment can serve many WhatsApp numbers. Each number is a `sendo_accounts` row with its `phone_number_id`, `waba_id`, its own token env var (`token_ref`), a `timezone` and an optional `tenant_id` (for example one number per clinic or building). Every contact, conversation and message copies the account’s `tenant_id`.

- Contacts are unique per account and phone: the same person writing to two tenants’ numbers becomes two contacts, each with its own history.
- Set `active = false` to stop routing and sending for a number without deleting its data.

## Adding numbers

```shell
# .env.local / deployment env
SENDO_TOKEN_CLINICA_NORTE=...
SENDO_TOKEN_CLINICA_SUR=...

npx @quami/sendo accounts add --phone-number-id 111111111111111 --token-env SENDO_TOKEN_CLINICA_NORTE \
  --tenant-id 6f1c0c3e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001 --timezone America/Guatemala --yes
npx @quami/sendo accounts add --phone-number-id 222222222222222 --token-env SENDO_TOKEN_CLINICA_SUR \
  --tenant-id 6f1c0c3e-0000-4000-8000-000000000002 --yes
```

Numbers in different WABAs can use different tokens; numbers in the same WABA can share one env var. Then subscribe each WABA’s webhook ([Meta setup](https://sendo.dev/docs/meta-setup#webhook)) and run `doctor`, or `doctor --account <id>` for one.

## Inbound routing

All numbers share one webhook URL. Each change in a payload carries `metadata.phone_number_id`, which is looked up in `sendo_accounts`:

- Active match: processed for that account and tenant.
- No match or inactive: the event is marked `unrouted`, a warning is logged, the `event.unrouted` event fires, and nothing else is written. Add the account and `sendo.events.reprocess(id)` it.

```ts title="ts"
// Replies to inbound messages go out from the number that received them.
sendo.on("message", async ({ account, reply }) => {
  console.log("received on", account.displayPhone, "tenant", account.tenantId);
  await reply.text("Recibido");
});
```

## Sending from a number

With exactly one active account, sends use it by default. With more than one, every `sendo.send.*` and `sendo.templates.sync` call must pass `account`: the Sendo account id, the Meta phone number id, or the `Account` object. Otherwise the call throws `AmbiguousAccountError` (or `AccountNotFoundError` for an unknown or inactive one). Replies (`reply`, agents, `sendo.inbox.reply`) always go out from the conversation’s own number.

```ts title="ts"
// With more than one active account, every send names its account:
// the sendo account id (uuid), the Meta phone_number_id, or the Account object.
await sendo.send.template(patientPhone, "recordatorio_cita", {
  account: tenantPhoneNumberId,
  language: "es",
  variables: ["Ana", "mañana 10:00"],
});
await sendo.send.text(patientPhone, "Te esperamos.", { account: tenantPhoneNumberId });
await sendo.templates.sync({ account: tenantPhoneNumberId });
```

```ts title="ts"
try {
  await sendo.send.text(patientPhone, "Hola"); // no account
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof AmbiguousAccountError) console.error(error.candidates); // account ids
}
```

## Agents per number

An agent’s `accounts` option is a list of account ids / phone number ids or a predicate. Only one agent may match each account: overlapping lists throw `ConfigError` at registration; overlaps found later (predicates, new accounts) are logged and no agent answers on that account until you fix them. The prompt uses the account’s `timezone` unless the agent sets one.

```ts title="ts"
const model = "openai/gpt-5-mini";
const surTenantId = "6f1c0c3e-0000-4000-8000-000000000002";

sendo.agent({ name: "norte", accounts: ["111111111111111"], model, instructions: "…" });
sendo.agent({
  name: "sur",
  accounts: (account) => account.tenantId === surTenantId,
  model,
  instructions: "…",
});
```

Full agent options: [API reference](https://sendo.dev/docs/api-reference#agents).

## Access per tenant

- Browser reads (inbox realtime) are filtered by `sendo_can_access_tenant(tenant_id)`: implement it with your membership table ([Quickstart step 4](https://sendo.dev/docs/quickstart#migration)).
- Server actions pass the user’s `tenantId` to `sendo.inbox.*`, and `linkContact` / `resolveHandoffTargets` receive the `account` so you can scope lookups by `account.tenantId`.

